Pseudo-diff F3 (seam_fp, nothing applied): a read time that counts the device's line before arrival.
Switch SGLANG_HICACHE_NEXT_TURN_READ_LINE (EnvBool False); deadline read order only. Under expected-cost timing
it must come with F2 (replay: without c, 349 of campaign 34's 1,525 late-run decisions become "start now").

Three parts.
 (1) Line: pages served before the read = launched reads (today's storage_read_backlog_pages) + parked reads due
     no later than this read's deadline ("now" reads always). Today only the hold sees parked reads
     (dispatch's ahead_pages, storage_read_scheduler.py:136-143); the planner before arrival and the queue
     check see launched pages only (unified_radix_cache.py:2334-2337).
 (2) Lags measured, not seeded: L3LoadModel's alloc_lag_s 0.5 s + drain_lag_s 0.36 s + read_fixed_s 0.044 s are
     dense-load seeds with one read ahead folded in. Measured in campaign 34 (out_f3_read_path.txt): lookup
     answered -> parked 14-17 ms; I/O end -> inserted 11-18 ms; with an idle read thread dispatch -> landed is
     pages x ms/page to within -16..-54 ms (median), 0.92 s under the model. Counting the line and keeping the
     seeds would count the read ahead twice.
 (3) Write hold: while timed reads are write-held, add what is left of a typical hold.

