What F3 does not do: it does not see reads that will be parked later with earlier deadlines (arrivals' own "now"
reads), so under a saturated read thread it still under-estimates; campaign 34's line was 42 s at the median in
minutes 90-110 with 27-43 reads parked (out_pr1_c34_*.txt). With F2 that no longer starts reads early: c is 0 there.
